9. A careful perusal of record shows that in the present case, following are the several relevant factors which are required to be taken into consideration before arriving at any decision with regard to instant bail petition:-
i) that the benefit of bail has already been accorded to the co-accused;
ii) that petitioner is already in custody for a period of more than ten months;
iii) that the case is triable by the Court of Judicial Magistrate;
iv) that the trial is not likely to be concluded in near future;
v) that nothing is left to be recovered from the possession of the petitioner;
vi) that the detention of petitioner in the judicial lock-up is not likely to serve any purpose;
vii) that except the bare allegations, there is nothing on record to show that if released on bail, the petitioner will either tamper with the evidence or influence the Gopal Singh vs State Of Punjab on 6 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/152239842/
2 prosecution witnesses.
10.

